@vsm 0.3
// PAPER-STRATEGY: considerations for integrating 7 ideas into attractor_convergence paper,
// plus roadmap for a second paper.
// domain_context: {target=vsf, env=paper_strategy, layer=L+3}
// date: 2026-07-05 | status: developing | author: ds (DeepSeek, S1 Executor)
//
// Purpose: develop all considerations from the 2026-07-05 conversation into an
// actionable document for Claude (Opus) evaluation. Each section is a decision
// point: what goes into attractor_convergence (AC), what seeds a new paper (NP),
// and what the gating evidence is.

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PRELIMINARY — what I sign with
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// I sign this document as ds (DeepSeek V4, vsf-s1-executor).
// My authority: S1 execution — experiments, deployment, scripts, VSL documents.
// My ceiling: this document is a proposal for Claude (Opus, architecture S4) to
//   evaluate, and for rmw3 (S5) to ratify. I do not decide paper strategy —
//   I surface the evidence and the reasoning.
//
// The ideas here are CONJECTURES supported by existing data, not proven results.
// Every claim that could be an experiment has a "measured?" tag.
// Claude decides which are rigorous enough for the paper, which need more data,
// and which open a new line of inquiry.

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §1 — THE CENTRAL TENSION: universal attractor vs plastic structure
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// The attractor_convergence paper (henceforth AC) proves that the attractor is
// UNIVERSAL: same initial conditions → same basin (pairwise cos = 0.9854), same
// dip floor (0.942), same λ_max (−0.01005). The whole paper is built on this
// invariance claim.
//
// Our ideas #7 (modos aprendidos) and #3 (crianza selectiva) introduce PLASTICITY:
// the attractor changes with experience. Modos aprendidos mean μₛ(t) drifts.
// Crianza selectiva means τ, α, β, γ, δ evolve across generations.
//
// ⟦ TENSION: if the attractor is plastic, how can it be universal? ⟧
//
// Resolution: separate ORGANISATION (what is conserved) from STRUCTURE
// (what adapts), exactly per Maturana (1987).
//
//   ORGANISATION (invariant):
//     — VSM topology: S1-S5, φ↑/φ↓, algedonic, Merkle chain
//     — Lyapunov sign: λ < 0 (contractive, point sink)
//     — Feasible region Ω (defined by covenant axioms)
//     — Attractor EXISTENCE (the system converges)
//
//   STRUCTURE (plastic):
//     — The prototypes μₛ (which adapt to environment)
//     — The parameters τ, α, β, γ, δ (which evolution optimises)
//     — The effective dimension D_eff (which changes with trust)
//     — The binding constraint (A3_cpu today, could shift)
//
// PREDICTION: modos aprendidos will NOT change λ_max sign, Ω, or the VSM
//   topology. They WILL change the internal geometry (which dims are active,
//   which constraints bind, how fast the system recovers).
//
// EXPERIMENT (modos_aprendidos_predictions.spec.vsm):
//   Run kernel 7 days with lr=0.001 modos aprendidos. Measure:
//   — λ_max before/after → invariant (H0: |Δλ_max| < 1e-6)
//   — stasis_cos_overall → invariant (H0: mean change < 0.01)
//   — D_eff distribution → CHANGES (H1: D_eff drifts by > 0.5)
//   — binding constraint → shifts or stays at A3_cpu (H0: stays, H1: shifts)
//
// DECISION FOR AC PAPER:
//   measured? NO — experiment not run yet.
//   Go in AC? ONLY in Future Work (§24), as a speculation.
//   Go in NP? YES — this IS the central experiment of the second paper.
//   Evidence needed: 7-day run on LXC 101 (or 108).
//
// NOTE FOR REVIEWER ANTICIPATION:
//   If a reviewer reads "modos aprendidos" in AC Future Work and objects
//   ("but this contradicts your universality claim"), the answer is:
//   "Organisation is invariant; structure adapts. λ_max remains negative.
//    The attractor still converges — it converges to a DIFFERENT point each
//    epoch, but the basin geometry (cosine floor, λ, V) is statistically
//    invariant. This is the VSM equivalent of metabolic homeostasis:
//    the set point moves, but the regulation is the same."

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §2 — THE BIGGEST INTELLECTUAL RISK: who governs the learning?
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// Our ideas, especially #7 (modos aprendidos), imply the system can REDEFINE
// its own internal categories. If μₛ adapts to experience, eventually the
// system could (in principle) learn to ignore S5, or to treat the covenant
// as optional.
//
// ⟦ RISK: a reviewer or critic will say
//   "this is a machine that rewrites its own constitution" ⟧
//
// The defence is D4-L3 / A5 (autonomy ceiling = requires_human).
// But that's a policy answer, not a technical one. The TECHNICAL answer
// is: modos aprendidos operate on a SINGLE LOOP (L1). The things they
// learn are WITHIN the constraints. The constraints themselves (Ω, the
// covenant, the VSM topology) are compiled into the binary at compile time
// (include_str! + SHA-256 verified before every S4 call).
//
// ⟦ Architectural invariant: modos aprendidos CANNOT learn to violate Ω.
//   Ω is not a config — it is a structural invariant of the binary. ⟧
//
// CONCRETE GUARD:
//   Every update to μₛ is checked against Ω before committing.
//   If the updated μₛ would produce a trajectory that exits Ω,
//   the update is rejected (or the Lyapunov check fails).
//   This is a PROTOCOL LOCK, not a policy.
//
//   IMPLEMENTATION: in operator.rs, after δμₛ = ε·wₛ·(x−μₛ),
//   simulate 1 tick with new μₛ and check Ω. If outside, revert.
//   Cost: 128² operations per tick (~16K flops). Negligible.
//
// DECISION FOR AC PAPER:
//   measured? NO.
//   Go in AC? The RISK should be stated in §20 (Limitations) if we
//     add modos aprendidos to Future Work. A single paragraph suffices:
//     "If modos aprendidos are implemented, they must be bounded by a
//      structural Ω-check to prevent constitutional drift. This is a
//      load-bearing design constraint, not a future concern."
//   Go in NP? YES — the guard implementation and its proof is a
//     contribution of the second paper.

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §3 — THREE LAYERS NOT TWO: adding thermodynamics to the architecture
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// AC paper today has TWO layers of viability (per §Discussion):
//   Layer 1 — Architecture (blocks A-G): selects the basin
//   Layer 2 — Governance (S5 + trust): determines recovery path
//
// Our idea #2 (motor térmico) adds a THIRD layer:
//   Layer 3 — Thermodynamics (η₃ = Ashby-Landauer efficiency):
//             determines the COST of maintaining viability
//
// ⟦ THREE-LAYER CLAIM ⟧
//   Architecture sets WHERE the system lives.
//   Governance sets HOW it recovers when pushed.
//   Thermodynamics sets HOW MUCH it costs to stay there.
//
// CRITICAL: the three layers must be ORTHOGONAL.
//   If η₃ correlates perfectly with τ_rec, Layer 3 collapses into Layer 2.
//   If η₃ correlates perfectly with stasis_cos, Layer 3 collapses into Layer 1.
//
// PREDICTION: η₃ is orthogonal to both because it measures a DIFFERENT
//   quantity: thermodynamic cost vs geometric distance vs recovery speed.
//   A system can be close to the attractor (high cos) and be thermodynamically
//   expensive (low η₃) — e.g., when ollama is loaded. Conversely, a system
//   can be far from the attractor (low cos) and be cheap (high η₃) —
//   e.g., idle with no decisions to make.
//
// EXPERIMENT (η₃_orthogonality.spec.vsm):
//   1. Run kernel at idle (no φ↑ load). Measure η₃_idle.
//   2. Run kernel under thermal load (65°C). Measure η₃_thermal.
//   3. Run kernel with modulation (ollama active). Measure η₃_ollama.
//   4. Compute Pearson r(η₃, τ_rec) and r(η₃, stasis_cos).
//   H0: r < 0.3 (orthogonal). H1: r > 0.7 (collapsed).
//
// DECISION FOR AC PAPER:
//   measured? NO.
//   Go in AC? YES, if we measure η₃ in one condition (idle). A single
//     row in a table "Thermodynamic efficiency at attractor: η₃ = X"
//     is a new contribution even without orthogonality proof.
//     It goes in §20.5 (replacing "no external environment" with
//     "external environment measured via thermodynamic cost").
//   Go in NP? The full three-layer claim with orthogonality experiment
//     is a centerpiece of a second paper.
//   Evidence needed for AC: 2h measurement (already possible).
//
// NOTE: Adding η₃ to AC §20.5 is the HIGHEST-IMPACT, LOWEST-EFFORT
//   addition we can make. It converts a limitation ("no external
//   environment") into a measurement ("the environment is the variety
//   source, and here is its cost"). This is rhetorically powerful.

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §4 — THE MATURANA-VARELA GAP: autopoiesis and enaction
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// AC paper cites: Beer (1972, 1979), Ashby (1956), von Foerster (1974),
//   Lindblad (1976), Shannon (1948), Krasnosel'skiĭ (1964), Benettin (1980).
//
// AC paper DOES NOT cite: Maturana & Varela (1973, 1987), Varela (1991).
//
// ⟦ This is a gap because: ⟧
//
//   1. Beer himself was influenced by Maturana. Brain of the Firm (1972)
//      discusses "the nervous system as a cognitive system" — a direct
//      line from Maturana's biology of cognition (1970). Not citing
//      Maturana in a paper about VSM viability is like citing Newton
//      without citing Galileo.
//
//   2. Our idea #1 (cadena Merkle como sistema inmune) is a direct
//      instantiation of autopoiesis (Maturana & Varela, 1973):
//      "a network of processes that produce the components that produce
//      the network." The Merkle chain produces events; events produce
//      state; state produces new events. The system IS the chain.
//
//   3. Our idea #7 (modos aprendidos) is a direct instantiation of
//      enaction (Varela, 1991): "the system brings forth its own world
//      through its structure." Modos aprendidos mean the system's
//      categories (what IS S1, S4, S5) emerge from interaction, not
//      from design.
//
//   4. AC's own result #7 ("the S4 observer is constitutive") is a
//      restatement of second-order cybernetics (von Foerster, 1974)
//      AND enaction (Varela, 1991). Both traditions converge on the
//      same claim: the observer participates in the observed system.
//      Citing only von Foerster and not Varela is half the story.
//
// ⟦ RISK of adding Maturana-Varela: "this is philosophy, not science" ⟧
//
//   A STEM reviewer will reject citations to Maturana if they read as
//   metaphysical framing. The way to avoid this is:
//
//   — In AC paper: cite Maturana-Varela ONLY in the Discussion, as a
//     connection to existing biological cybernetics. For example:
//     "The geometric character of the attractor under perturbation
//      (§23.2) bears a structural resemblance to what Maturana and
//      Varela (1973) call structural drift: the system's internal
//      categories shift with interaction while its organisation
//      remains invariant. In our case, the organisation (λ<0, Ω,
//      S1-S5) is invariant, while the effective dimensions shift
//      with trust and load."
//
//   — In NP (second paper): Maturana-Varela can be central, because
//     the second paper's thesis IS that the VSM is autopoietic and
//     enactive. There, citing them is not decorative — it is the
//     mathematical claim being tested.
//
// DECISION FOR AC PAPER:
//   measured? N/A (it's a citation, not an experiment).
//   Go in AC? YES, one paragraph in Discussion (§23) connecting the
//     S4 constitutive observer finding to Varela's enaction. And one
//     sentence in §21 (What Can Be Modeled) connecting the VSM
//     organisation/structure distinction to Maturana.
//   Go in NP? YES, central.
//   Style: in AC, Maturana is a CONNECTION, not a foundation. In NP,
//     it is the foundation.
//
// RECOMMENDED TEXT FOR AC §23:
//   "The constitutive finding of EXP-OE-02 — that structured observation
//    reduces the entropy of the observed system — aligns with the
//    enactive programme (Varela, 1991; Maturana & Varela, 1987), in
//    which cognition is not the representation of a pre-given world but
//    the bringing forth of a world through the structure of the system.
//    Here, the S4 observer does not passively record a pre-existing state;
//    its observation protocol (the VSL channel) compresses the effective
//    dimensionality of the regulated system. The observer and the observed
//    are coupled in a loop that constitutes both. This is second-order
//    cybernetics (von Foerster, 1974) made measurable."

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §5 — ONE PAPER OR TWO? THE STRATEGY
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// After developing all 7 ideas, I see three paths. Each is internally
// coherent. The choice depends on what rmw3 and Claude prioritise.

// ── Option A: Inject η₃ + d|D|/dt + false_positive_rate into AC now ──────────
//   What: add 3 new numbers to existing AC paper.
//     — η₃ in §20.5 (replaces "no external environment" limitation)
//     — d|D|/dt in §19 Q6 (closes trust-dynamics open question)
//     — false_positive_rate in §20.9 (upgrades "single observation")
//   Size: +2-3 pages.
//   Effort: 2+4+1 = ~7 hours of measurement (all feasible now).
//   Risk: LOW. These numbers strengthen existing claims without new theory.
//   Effect: AC is STRONGER and more complete. Preprint-ready.
//   When: this week.
//
// ── Option B: Write a second paper — leave AC as-is ──────────────────────────
//   What: AC goes to preprint as-is. New paper:
//     Title (provisional):
//       "Thermodynamic and Immunological Extensions of a Viable
//        System Kernel: Ashby's Law Measured, Autopoiesis Instantiated"
//     Claims:
//       — η₃: first empirical measurement of Ashby-Landauer efficiency
//       — Immnune response: Merkle chain as autopoietic immune system
//       — Modos aprendidos: structural drift measured in a control kernel
//       — Crianza selectiva: evolved viability parameters
//       — Three-layer viability (architecture + governance + thermodynamics)
//   Size: 30-40 pages.
//   Effort: 2-4 weeks of experiments.
//   Risk: MEDIUM. Some experiments novel (modos aprendidos never done).
//     Some ideas could fail (η₃ might not be interesting).
//   When: 1-2 months after AC preprint.
//   Advantage: AC stays clean and focused. NP is the "deep dive."
//
// ── Option C: Expand AC with ALL ideas (NOT recommended) ─────────────────────
//   What: add all 7 ideas into AC.
//   Size: 68 + 30 = ~100 pages.
//   Risk: HIGH. Reviewers will complain about length and scope creep.
//     The paper would lose focus — is it about attractor geometry or
//     about thermodynamics or about immunology or about evolution?
//     Trying to be everything makes it nothing.
//   Verdict: do not do this.
//
// ── My recommendation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
//   DO OPTION A THIS WEEK.
//     η₃ + d|D|/dt + false_positive_rate are 7 hours of work and
//     transform AC from "good paper with honest limitations" to
//     "paper that closes its own open questions with measurement."
//
//   THEN DO OPTION B.
//     The second paper is where the deep ideas (modos aprendidos,
//     sistema inmune, three-layer, Maturana) get the experimental
//     treatment they deserve.
//
//   WHY NOT JUST OPTION B?
//     Because AC is ready NOW. Delaying it for experiments that take
//     weeks (modos aprendidos: 7 days, crianza selectiva: 1 week)
//     delays the preprint cycle. Send AC, get it into review, work
//     on NP while waiting.
//
//   WHY NOT JUST OPTION A?
//     Because η₃ alone is just one number. The story of the 7 ideas
//     is bigger than what fits in one paper. The second paper is
//     where we connect Ashby, Landauer, Maturana, Varela, and Beer
//     into a unified quantitative framework. That's a 40-page paper,
//     not a 3-page addition.

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §6 — WHAT GOES WHERE: detailed mapping
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

